# examples/B1/alpha.mac with QBBC's hadronic processes switched off.
#
# For the real Geant4 build of B1 only. This port has no hadronic physics, so comparing its
# answer against a full QBBC run measures that absence rather than the transport; this macro
# removes it from the Geant4 side so the two are running the same physics.
#
# Switched off by UI command rather than by editing B1's physics list, because B1's physics
# list is the thing being kept identical. /process/inactivate is Geant4's own supported way to
# do this and it leaves the tables and the cuts exactly as QBBC built them.
#
# Everything below the inactivations is character for character examples/B1/alpha.mac.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/process/inactivate hadElastic
/process/inactivate alphaInelastic
/process/inactivate ionElastic
/process/inactivate ionInelastic

/gun/particle alpha
/gun/energy 840 MeV

/run/printProgress 2000
/run/beamOn 10000
